## Contents:     Default productions for selection problem space for Soar 9.6.3
##  1. in evaluation substate, copy the desireds.desired instead of the desireds <d> pointer
##     important because substates add and remove achieved flags which become o-supported
###########################################################################
##  1. Changed ^desired to ^desireds.desired so can support multiple desired conditions (many changes)
##  2. Add ^achieved true as an augmentation of individual desireds.
##  3. Updated datamap to remove errors
###########################################################################
##  1. Added rule that cover failures in the selection space
##     default*select*reject*conflict
##
#############################################################################
##  Checked and tested for 9.6.1 
##  1. Has datamap warnings for variable attributes
##
###########################################################################
##  Changes made in Soar 9.6.0
##   1. Modified state representations to include ^world for all task data
##      only world information is copied to evaluation substate. 
##      many rules changed in section 7.3.2.1 State Copying
##   
###########################################################################
##  Change made for Soar 9.3
##   1. Added expected-value as a result - these get translated into numeric preferences
#########################################################################
##  Change made for Soar 9.0 
##   Added exhaustion-failure so could make sure no attempts to chunk over it.
##   1. modify top-goal*halt*failure
##   2. add selection*select*exhaustion-failure-evaluation-becomes-reject-preference
##   3. modify evaluate-operator*elaborate*symbolic-evaluation*from-subgoal
##   4. modify evaluate-operator*elaborate*evaluation*from-subgoal*duplicate-desired
##   5. modify monitor*goal*failure
##   6. evaluate-operator*elaborate*evaluation*failure*constraint-failure
##   7. evaluate-operator*elaborate*evaluation*failure*no-operators
##   8. selection*elaborate*state*all-objects-evaluated mod so not test for non evaluate-operator
########################################################################
### Change made for Soar 8.5
###
### Significant Changes made to Convert to Soar 8.2
###    1. evaluate-object -> evaluate-operator
###    2. Removed other types of evaulate-
###    3. Change from problem-space.name selection -> name selection
###    4. Simplified so only handles vanillia evaluate-operator
###    5. Don't copy down problem space, just copy down name and
###       assume problem space will be regenerated in subgoal based on name
###    6. Added some documentation
###    

###

###    State structure:
###    (state <s> ^evaluation <evaluation>
###               ^not-all-operators-evaulated true
###               ^operator-selection not-indifferent
###               ^found-value true)
###    (<evaluation> ^numeric-value  no-value
###         ^expected-al
###         ^symbolic-value no-value/success/failure
###         ^value true
###         ^operator (identifier of operator being evaluated)
###         ^desireds <desired>
###
###
###    (<operator> ^name evaluate-operator
###         ^operator <super-operator>
###         ^evaluation <evaluation>  ;# same as on state
###         ^super-problem-space
###         ^superstate 

### (19 Nov 2026, v2.45: the no-local-negations mode below is removed from selection-world; ^no-local-negations is no longer tested.)
### Changes May 2007 (SBW):
### Added a 'no local negations' mode. If the problem space has a ^no-local-negations flag, rules will be used 
### that avoid local negations, supporting versions of Soar that refuse to chunk over local negations.
### There are a number of assumptions that must hold for this mode to work, though:
###
###  ^default-operator-copy yes must be on the problem-space
###  ^default-state-copy yes must be on the problem-space
###  ^default-desired-copy yes is not supported
###  ^dont-copy and ^dont-copy-anything are not supported
###  all-attributes-at-level mode are not supported
###  attributes on task operators cannot refer to attributes attached to the state
###  the state must be a tree-- no value can be referred to by multiple attributes

# Not needed in 9.6.3
#chunk singleton state superstate-set state
#chunk singleton operator super-problem-space identifier
#chunk singleton operator super-operator operator
#chunk singleton any top-state any
#chunk singleton any superstate any   # the architectural one doesn't apply to operators 
#chunk singleton any numeric-value any
#chunk singleton any symbolic-value any
#chunk singleton any expected-value any
#chunk singleton any super-operator any
#chunk singleton any found-value any
#chunk singleton any operator-selection any
#chunk singleton any evaluation any
#chunk singleton any duplicate-of any
#chunk singleton any super-problemspace any
#chunk singleton any look-ahead-operator any
#chunk singleton any untried-tied-operator any
#chunk singleton any tried-tied-operator any
#chunk singleton any name identifier

multi-attributes evaluation 5
